; Dungeons: a named group of levels reached through a world-map location.
;
; The tier that did not exist before the world map (docs/world-map.md). Until
; now a "dungeon" was only an accident of which level stems' stairs happened to
; point at each other, and project.ini's flat `levels` list was the whole
; hierarchy. That list STAYS — it is the editor's universe — and a dungeon
; simply names which of those levels belong to it.
;
; A DUNGEON IS NOT A PLACE. The world-map LOCATION is the place; this is the
; content behind it. That is what lets a found map reveal a location without
; touching the dungeon, and what would let two locations share one dungeon.
;
; Fields:
;   levels   space-separated level stems, in depth order. Every stem must exist
;            in project.ini.
;   entry    the level a party arriving from the world map lands on. Must be one
;            of `levels`; defaults to the first.
;   tags     flavour, for later content matching (Catalog.h tags).

[waystation]
display = The Waystation
; The demo's composed level, and the two gallery floors beneath it. `showcase`
; leads because that is where a new game has always opened.
levels = showcase start level2
entry = showcase
tags = stone
